Relation to `--layers`: tiers outer, per-library layers nested inside each
tier. Two libraries, `z_base` and `a_app` (`a_app` depends on `z_base`, so
`z_base`'s rules come first in dependency order); each has one base atom
and one conditional (`:hover`) atom.

  $ mkdir a_app z_base

  $ cat > z_base/z_base.ml <<EOF
  > [@@@css.config [("library-name", "z_base")]]
  > [@@@css ".a-zbase{color:red;}"]
  > [@@@css ".a-zbasehover:hover{color:darkred;}"]
  > let widget () = ()
  > EOF

  $ cat > a_app/main.ml <<EOF
  > [@@@css.config [("library-name", "a_app")]]
  > [@@@css ".a-aapp{color:blue;}"]
  > [@@@css ".a-aapphover:hover{color:darkblue;}"]
  > let _ = Z_base.widget
  > EOF

Without `--layers`: the usual two tiers, no library nesting - both
libraries' base atoms share one `styled-ppx.base` block (in dependency
order), both `:hover` atoms share one `styled-ppx.conditional` block.

  $ styled-ppx.generate a_app/main.ml z_base/z_base.ml
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  @layer styled-ppx.global, styled-ppx.descendant, styled-ppx.base, styled-ppx.conditional;
  @layer styled-ppx.base {
  .a-zbase{color:red;}
  .a-aapp{color:blue;}
  }
  @layer styled-ppx.conditional {
  .a-zbasehover:hover{color:darkred;}
  .a-aapphover:hover{color:darkblue;}
  }

With `--layers`: the SAME two outer tiers, each now carrying its own
NESTED `@layer z_base, a_app;` statement and per-library blocks - a
library's base atoms and its conditional atoms sit in the SAME relative
per-library order in both tiers, since each tier buckets by the same
`library_order`.

  $ styled-ppx.generate --layers a_app/main.ml z_base/z_base.ml
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  @layer styled-ppx.global, styled-ppx.descendant, styled-ppx.base, styled-ppx.conditional;
  @layer styled-ppx.base {
  @layer z_base, a_app;
  @layer z_base {
  .a-zbase{color:red;}
  }
  @layer a_app {
  .a-aapp{color:blue;}
  }
  }
  @layer styled-ppx.conditional {
  @layer z_base, a_app;
  @layer z_base {
  .a-zbasehover:hover{color:darkred;}
  }
  @layer a_app {
  .a-aapphover:hover{color:darkblue;}
  }
  }

What the browser does now, and why: nesting `@layer z_base { ... }` inside
`@layer styled-ppx.base { ... }` (and again inside `styled-ppx.conditional`)
gives each pair its own, separate cascade-layer identity - `z_base`'s
conditional atom never has to out-rank `a_app`'s base atom by accident,
since the OUTER `styled-ppx.base`/`styled-ppx.conditional` order already
settled base-vs-conditional before any library ordering is even
consulted; library order only ever decides ties WITHIN one tier, exactly
as `--layers` already did before tiers existed.
